%TC=3.                               Bundle Menu Help.
%TC=7.
At this menu you can choose to either...
%TC=6.
%TC=7.1) DOWNLOAD%TC=6. messages you have selected.
%TC=7.2) UPLOAD%TC=6. a reply message packet from your QWK-Offline reader.
%TC=7.3) UPDATE%TC=6. on/off 'last-read' pointer flag.
%TC=7.4) GOTO%TC=6. Message Area selection Menu.
%TC=7.5) QUIT%TC=6. QWK bundler and return back to the BBS.
%TC=7.
1. DOWNLOAD:
%TC=6.
Before choosing this selection you should confirm...
a) You have selected all the message areas and message numbers that you
want.
b) The 'TOTAL MARKED:' number is less than the 'LIMIT IS:' number. (If not
you will be given an option to only bundle upto your limit. (Currently 500
messages) Or to re-select the message areas and quantities.
Once you have successfully started the message downloading your messages
will be Arced up and you will be prompted to start your file transfer.
The messages will be in a file called "CHIBA.QWK" This file will be
compressed by LHARC. Your QWK message reader should detect this archive
method automatically.
%TC=7.
2. UPLOAD:
%TC=6.
You should only choose this option when you have a message packet that is a
reply to a message bundle that you downloaded from THIS BBS. You cannot
upload a mail packet that replies to a QWK bundle from another BBS. The
reason being that the message area numbering will be totally different!
Also your reply packet will have to be Archived up in LHARC format.
If you have a packet that complies with the above, then choose this option
and follow the prompts. Your replies will then be automatically inserted
into the proper message areas automatically.
%TC=7.
3. UPDATE: (Last-Read)
%TC=6.
This is an important option that will decide whether your 'last-read'
pointers for a message area will be updated or not. Normally you will want
this option ON so that when you next bundle up messages you will know where
you 'last-read' upto last time. Your last-read pointers are used to
automatically set the 'start' pointers for message bundling. Although you
can manually over-ride this and set your own 'start' position. (See the
'Areas' help file for details.)
%TC=7.
4. GOTO: Message Area Menu
%TC=6.
You should choose this option when you want to reselect and edit message
areas to bundle from.
NOTE: If you have selected more than the maximum allowed number of messages
(500) there is no need for YOU to restrict the numbers...this will be done
automatically. - You can simply start the download and UPTO a maximum of 500
messages will be bundled.
%TC=7.
5. QUIT: (Back to BBS)
%TC=6.
If you want to quit the QWK bundler then simply choose this option and you
will exit back to the BBS.
%TC=7.
